        {
          "title": "Series and DataFrame Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Series",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==1-D labelled array==: values + index",
                "**One dtype** for the whole Series"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. DataFrame",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==2-D table==",
                "Each column is a **Series**",
                "All columns share **one row index**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import pandas as pd",
                "df = pd.DataFrame({'name': ['A','B'], 'age': [30, 25]})"
              ],
              "note": "dict keys become column names"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Attribute",
                "Gives"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`df.shape`",
                  "(rows, cols)"
                ],
                [
                  "`df.dtypes`",
                  "type per column"
                ],
                [
                  "`df.columns`",
                  "column labels"
                ],
                [
                  "`df.index`",
                  "row labels"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Alignment",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`s1 + s2` matches by ==label==, not position",
                "Label in only one Series gives {red:NaN}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Alignment",
              "text": "Missing labels never raise an error; they give ==NaN==."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Series vs DataFrame?** 1-D vs 2-D; a DataFrame is Series sharing one index",
                "**s1 + s2 with different labels?** Matches by label; unmatched give NaN",
                "**Does df.shape count the index?** No, only (rows, cols)"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
