    {
      "title": "Selecting Columns, loc vs iloc",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Selecting Columns, loc vs iloc",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Picking Columns",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df['col']` → a ==Series==",
                "`df[['a','b']]` (a list) → a ==DataFrame==",
                "Double brackets keep the 2-D shape"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. loc vs iloc",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "loc",
                "iloc"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Selects by",
                  "**label**",
                  "**integer position**"
                ],
                [
                  "Slice end",
                  "{green:inclusive}",
                  "{red:exclusive}"
                ],
                [
                  "`df[...][0:2]` rows",
                  "`df.loc[0:2]` → 3",
                  "`df.iloc[0:2]` → 2"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Same pattern for both: `[rows, cols]`",
                "Examples below: label, position, then all rows with a column range"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.loc[5, 'age']       # label",
                "df.iloc[0, 1]          # position",
                "df.loc[:, 'a':'c']     # all rows, cols a to c"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Assigning",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Do}: `df.loc[df['age'] > 30, 'senior'] = True`",
                "{red:Avoid}: `df[df['age'] > 30]['senior'] = True`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Chained indexing",
              "text": "`df[...]['col'] = x` ==never changes df==. It writes to a temporary copy. Use one `loc` call."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Boolean Filtering and Index Control",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Boolean Filtering and Index Control",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Boolean Mask",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df[df['age'] > 30]` builds a ==boolean Series== mask",
                "Keeps only the rows where the mask is {green:True}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Combine and Test",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Op",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`&`",
                  "and"
                ],
                [
                  "`|`",
                  "or"
                ],
                [
                  "`~`",
                  "not"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wrap each condition in ==parentheses==",
                "With `&`, **both conditions must hold**",
                "`isin([...])` tests membership",
                "`str.contains('an')` filters text"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df[(df.age > 30) & (df.city == 'NYC')]",
                "df[df['city'].isin(['NYC','LA'])]",
                "df[df['name'].str.contains('an')]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Index Control",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`set_index('id')` makes a column the ==index==",
                "`df.loc[101]` then looks up by that label",
                "`reset_index(drop=True)` restores ==0..n-1== after filtering or sorting"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df = df.set_index('id')",
                "df.loc[101]",
                "df = df.reset_index(drop=True)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`set_index` returns a new DataFrame. `reset_index` returns a new DataFrame; without `drop=True` the old index becomes a column."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Filter mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`and` / `or` on a Series raises =={red:truth value is ambiguous}",
                "Use `&`, `|`, `~` instead, with ==parentheses== around each condition",
                "`df.age > 30 & df.x == 1` runs in the wrong order and fails"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df[(df.age > 30) & (df.x == 1)]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Writes that vanish",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Mistake",
                "Result",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`df[df.a > 1]['b'] = 0`",
                  "df unchanged, `ChainedAssignmentError`",
                  "`df.loc[mask, 'b'] = 0`"
                ],
                [
                  "`set_index`, `reset_index`, `drop`",
                  "new object, change lost",
                  "`df = df.set_index('id')`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Index after filtering",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "The filtered rows keep their ==original labels==",
                "`loc` uses labels, `iloc` uses positions: different rows"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import pandas as pd",
                "df = pd.DataFrame({'a': [1, 5, 9]})",
                "sub = df[df.a > 1]",
                "print(sub.loc[1, 'a'], sub.iloc[1, 0])",
                "sub = sub.reset_index(drop=True)",
                "print(sub.loc[1, 'a'])"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "5 9",
                "9"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Need positions after a filter? `reset_index(drop=True)`. Always assign the result."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
